<title>ESTONIA: HUVITUSFOND ANNOUNCES NEW ISSUE.</title>
<headline>HUVITUSFOND ANNOUNCES NEW ISSUE.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Huvitusfond (Compensation Fund) on Wednesday announced the issue of its ninth series of bonds worth 30 million kroons.</p>
<p>The issue will take place between May 21 and June 18, it added in a statement.</p>
<p>Huvitusfond will set the minimum offer price of a 100 kroon face-value bond on May 20. The issue will be sold for vouchers.</p>
<p>The term of a bond is five years and the fund will buy the issue back on June 18 2002 at face value.</p>
<p>Huvitusfond will pay interest once a year, on June 18.</p>
<p>Huvitusfond had a profit of 63 million kroons in 1996, which is up from 32 million kroons the year before.</p>
<p>Its bonds are traded on the stock exchange.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn Newsroom, +372 630 8400, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
